  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A scan of the ground at the Osiris Shaft, a deep ancient shaft cut into the Giza plateau near the Egyptian pyramids, picks up something else on the shaft's left side, according to the researcher Jeffrey Drum. He describes this to Jesse Michels as part of a recent project using radar-style scans to look for hidden structures deep underground. If it holds up, it would hint at more buried construction beneath the plateau than is known."
